{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/58101-recruitment-werewolf-the-forsaken-unnamed-chronicle","id":58101,"title":"[recruitment][Werewolf: the Forsaken]unnamed chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T08:32:14-08:00","id":58101,"title":"[recruitment][Werewolf: the Forsaken]unnamed chronicle","content":"First time posting have been lurking for a couple of weeks. As the title says I am looking to start a WtF play by post chronicle here on these boards. I have been running PbP games for over two years on the Paizo boards. I will be using all updated rules, and including some of the older stuff on a case by case basis. The translation guides will be in effect. All supernatural creatures exists and you should expect to run into at least one of each over the course of play. Characters should be standard creation. They should NOT be part of the same pack at the beginning of the adventure. I expect all characters to detail parts of their current pack (the bare minimum I am willing to accept for this is name with tribe and auspice). I would like a minimum of three personal story hooks per character. The setting will be around the Pugent Sound to include Seattle, Bainbridge Island, Vashon Island, poulsbo, the Olympic National Forest, and Mt Rainer. Interests, questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:44:52-08:00","id":58177,"title":"","content":"Would the players have to have played PbP games before? I would LOVE to play, but I've never done PbP and would hate to ruin the fun by forcing you to explain how PbP works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But that would be *shudders* <i>fun</i>!<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/119-strapping-gent","name":"Strapping Gent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T12:38:59-08:00","id":58248,"title":"","content":"No problem if you haven't done pbp before. It is a medium that allows greater role play but is much slower paced. The only requirement that I have is you post at least once a day. Until I can find a good site for online dice rolls I will handle then myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:42:33-08:00","id":58397,"title":"","content":"Well than I'm all for it! How soon do you want characters, or will you wait until there are more players to tell them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But that would be *shudders* <i>fun</i>!<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/119-strapping-gent","name":"Strapping Gent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:06:53-08:00","id":58406,"title":"","content":"I want at least two more players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:30:02-08:00","id":59259,"title":"","content":"I know this is a relatively new forum but are there any more interested in starting an Uratha presence on these boards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:24:50-08:00","id":61694,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested, but I'm curious as to what you mean by &quot;all updated rules&quot;? Also never played a PbP game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T14:29:32-08:00","id":61747,"title":"","content":"GMC rules update and no pbp experience is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:43:04-08:00","id":62523,"title":"","content":"Okay, that's two I just want one more and we can start the prep work for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:10:12-08:00","id":66895,"title":"","content":"I might be interested in playing a game of Werewolf the Forsaken with you, DaWay. But first, could you tell us a bit more about this campaign's setting? I would like to know what are the house rules for this as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 02-06-2014, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T09:03:13-08:00","id":68461,"title":"","content":"The setting will be NW Washington state. A smaller city such as Bellingham or a town like poulsbo. You will meet all supernatural characters and I will be using god machine rules updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T22:20:40-08:00","id":69639,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply, DaWay. I've sent you a private message, you'll find my character concept in there. Perhaps you can help me develop it somewhat, while we wait for the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T07:13:09-08:00","id":69823,"title":"","content":"Got the message. Now if I could only hear from ABenniton and Strapping Gent. Also I will not be using any of those house rules. I will be playing by the book. If anything needs to change we can discuss it as a group If the other two want to PM their characters I will open up an OOC thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:09:12-08:00","id":71886,"title":"","content":"Wait, how will you be playing it by the book, if the Idigam Chronicle hasn't been released yet? There's nothing in the God Machine Chronicles rule book that covers werewolves, except spirits of course, so why not use a homebrew rendition of those rules?<br /> <br /> I think those players have abandoned this thread, DaWay. Do you know anyone else who might be interested in playing Werewolf the Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 02-14-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:27:52-08:00","id":71942,"title":"","content":"No abandon, just haven't been near a computer for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But that would be *shudders* <i>fun</i>!<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/119-strapping-gent","name":"Strapping Gent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T22:55:09-08:00","id":72484,"title":"","content":"these updates:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion#post27026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reposting this from the old forums since there don't seem to be any other stopgap conversions that made the jump. As always, feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Werewolf: the Forsaken </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">God Machine Chronicle Update</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I borrowed some of the Uratha form changes from Pendragon, a poster on the Onyx Path forums.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Two of the new conditions are from the Blood and Smoke: Reap the Whirlwind quickstart. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Character Creation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Werewolves receive 10 merit points at character creation. The fifth dot of a trait does not cost two points.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Use the Virtue and Vice system from the GMC book. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Experience</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Attribute</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merit</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Totem</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skill Specialty</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skill</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Affinity Gift</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:: 3 Experiences per gift</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other Gift</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per gift</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Primary Renown</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other Renown</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Harmony</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Primal Urge</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rites</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Willpower</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Harmony</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Having seen the way Humanity is handled in Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, I have decided to leave Harmony as it is in the W:tF core rulebook, except instead of derangements, I will be adding custom conditions for Harmony rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Roll Results</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character\u2019s world view has been damaged, perhaps beyond repair. The character suffers from traumatic stress. Lose a dot of Harmony and choose from the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Broken, Fugue, or Spiritual Obsession. Also, take a Beat.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character\u2019s world view has been shaken and he probably questions his sense of self, his ability to relate to people, his own moral worth, or his sanity. Lose a dot of Harmony and choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Bestial, or Competitive.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character has come through the breaking point intact. He might feel guilty or upset about what happened, but he can cope. Choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Bestial, or Competitive.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:The character somehow manages not only to survive the breaking point, but to find meaning in it, to reaffirm his own self-worth, or to pass through fire and become tempered by it. The character takes a Beat and regains a point of Willpower.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Harmony Conditions</span></b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Bestial </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Your character acts on primal, physical impulses. Frightening things make him run. He meets aggressive threats with violence and anger. Take -2 to all rolls to resist frenzy or physical impulse. As well, take -2 to Defense due to impulsive action. Any rolls to compel your character to impulsive, aggressive action or escape achieve exceptional success on three successes instead of five. This could apply to Disciplines such as Nightmare, or Dominate under the right circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resolution: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Take an action during a frenzy that results in a breaking point. This Condition fades naturally after a number of days equal to your Primal Urge. After resolving Bestial, your character cannot be subject to this Condition again for a full month.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Beat: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">n/a</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Competitive </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Your character must assert dominance and superiority. Either she gives it her all, or she falters. Any time she\u2019s in direct competition with another character, she suffers -2 on any rolls where she doesn\u2019t spend Willpower. This includes contested rolls. As well, any rolls to tempt or coerce her into competition achieve exceptional success on three successes instead of five.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common Causes</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: A challenging predatory aura conflict, or a failed Detachment roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resolution</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Win or lose a competition where someone reaches a breaking point. This Condition fades naturally after a number of days equal to your Primal Urge. After resolving Competitive, your character cannot be subject to this Condition again for a full month.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Beat</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: n/a</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Spiritual Obsession</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The character gains a ban or compulsion as described on pages 185-186 of Werewolf: the Forsaken. She gains the 9-again quality on all rolls related to pursuing her obsession. On rolls that are unrelated to her obsession, she loses the 10-again quality. Obsession can be a temporary or persistent quality per Storyteller approval. Depending on the nature of the compulsion, the character may take a -2 on some social interactions. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Resolution</i>: The character sheds or purges her fixation by reaffirming her connection to humanity as a counterweight to her spiritual side.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Beat</i>: Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her obsession.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Uratha Forms</span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hishu (The Human): +2 to perception rolls.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dalu (The Near-Human): Strength +1, Stamina +1, Manipulation \u20131, Size +1, Health +2, Speed +1, +2 to perception rolls. 9-again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Can deal lethal damage unarmed.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gauru (The Wolfman): Rage invoked, Strength +3, Dexterity +1, Stamina +2, Size +2, Health +4, Initiative +1, Speed +4, Armor 1/1, inflict lethal damage (+1 bonus to claw attacks, +2 to bite attacks), +3 to perception rolls, wound penalties ignored and no unconsciousness rolls made, \u20132 to resist Death Rage, fail most Social and Mental tasks. 8 again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Urshul (The Near-Wolf): Strength +2, Dexterity +2, Stamina +2, Manipulation \u20133, Size +1, Health +3, Initiative +2, Speed +7, +3 to perception rolls, inflict lethal damage, 9-again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Urhan (The Wolf): Dexterity +2, Stamina +1, Size \u20131, Initiative +2, Speed +5, +4 to perception rolls, inflict lethal damage with bite attack. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2070-daway","name":"DaWay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:37:04-08:00","id":73280,"title":"","content":"The stopgap Mage rules have the players give their characters breaking points. Do you want us to do that as well, and if so what are the